The allegations are that the composition of the said Product exceeded therapeutic dose as under :-
a. Vitamin B6 Therapeutic dosage contained in the seized product was 20 mg whereas permissible range was 1.5 mg to 3 mg;
b. Folic Acid Therapeutic range is 1 mg to 1.5 mg whereas in product it was 0.8 mg;
c. Vitamin B12 Therapeutic dosage range is 5 mcg to 15 mcg whereas in product it in 0.5 mg (500 mcg).
4. Active ingredients exceeded limits as prescribed in Schedule V and also that the said product comes under purview of Section 3(b)(i) of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 and hence, it was a drug and not food, whereas the same was being sold under the FSSAI License no.10012062000165 as a food items only and not a Drug.
